{"name":"Turf Master","hex":"#009922","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A layer of earth covered with grass; sod.","A piece of such a layer cut from the soil. May be used as sod to make a lawn, dried for peat, stacked to form earthen structures, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with turf; to create a lawn by laying turfs.","To throw a frisbee well short of its intended target, usually causing it to hit the ground within 10 yards of its release."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turf"},{"term":"master","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who has control over something or someone.","The owner of an animal or slave."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Masterful.","Main, principal or predominant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/master"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sod","blocks":[{"text":"Sod is the upper layer of turf that is harvested for transplanting. Turf consists of a variable thickness of a soil medium that supports a community of turfgrasses. Sod is typically made with grasses that spread laterally through the soil and form a dense mat. In British and Australian English, sod is more commonly known as turf and the term sod is mainly used in agriculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rollrasen-01.jpg/330px-Rollrasen-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sod"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG/500px-Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG/1280px-Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG/500px-Anselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sod was historically used as a building material in various parts of the world, including settlers in the American grassland and in Scandinavia. Modern construction sometimes includes similar applications in green roofs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnselmo%2C_Nebraska_sod_house.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Golf_bunkers_Filton.jpg/500px-Golf_bunkers_Filton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Golf_bunkers_Filton.jpg/500px-Golf_bunkers_Filton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golf course sod","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGolf_bunkers_Filton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Harvesting_Sod.jpg/500px-Harvesting_Sod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Harvesting_Sod.jpg/1280px-Harvesting_Sod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Harvesting_Sod.jpg/500px-Harvesting_Sod.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Harvesting sod","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarvesting_Sod.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Trimax-Pegasus_Sod-Turf-Roller-Mower.jpg/500px-Trimax-Pegasus_Sod-Turf-Roller-Mower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Trimax-Pegasus_Sod-Turf-Roller-Mower.jpg/1280px-Trimax-Pegasus_Sod-Turf-Roller-Mower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org